'''G-LN''' was a [[DUM-series pit droid]] owned by [[Flix]] and [[Orka]]. G-LN assisted them in the [[Office of Acquisitions]] by helping them retrieve items or assist customers.

==Biography==
G-LN was manufactured by [[Serv-O-Droid, Inc.]]<ref name="Corr" /> and, at some point, was taken in by the [[Gozzo]] [[Flix]] and the [[Chadra-Fan]] [[Orka]].<ref name="RR">{{InsiderCite|190|Resistance Revisited|''Resistance'' Revisited}}</ref> The three worked together in [[Office of Acquisitions]], selling salvage aboard the ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Supertanker fuel depot|station]] on the [[planet]] [[Castilon]].<ref name="USWNE" />

===Managing Xiono===
{{Quote|[G-LN chitters]|formatting=0|G-LN greets BB-8, Neeku Vozo, and Kazuda Xiono|audio=GLNChitters-TheRecruit.flac|<ref name="Recruit" />}}
[[File:GLNWorking-TheRecruitPart2.png|thumb|250px|G-LN works while patrons visit Acquisitions.]]
In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="34ABY">{{ResistanceDate|1}}</ref> G-LN tinkered with some tools at the front desk of Acquisitions as [[Kadas'sa'Nikto]] [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Neeku Vozo]] and [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]], along with his [[BB-series astromech droid|droid]] companion [[BB-8]], arrived at the Office. The pit droid chittered to greet the patrons and, upon being shown a [[datapad]] with a list of parts from Vozo, banged on the desk and chittered loudly to the back to summon Flix and Orka, whom G-LN departed the seat at the desk for. When Vozo clarified they were looking for parts for his boss [[Jarek Yeager]]'s infamous [[Racing starfighter|ship]], the ''[[Fireball]]'', G-LN collapsed in laughter, believing Vozo was joking. Once the shopkeepers believed Vozo, they took the datapad from the [[Nikto]] and began compiling the requested components while G-LN followed with a bin to collect the merchandise.<ref name="Recruit" />

When Xiono confessed he could not [[Galactic Credit Standard|pay]] for the components, the shopkeepers stopped gathering the merchandise, and G-LN shook<ref name="Recruit" /> his<ref name="G-LN" /> head in disappointment. After a plea from Vozo, the partners agreed to trade some secondhand parts for a [[gorg]] for [[Diet|lunch]]. G-LN waved at the three patrons as they departed the office. When the trio later returned with a [[Bitey|gorg]], G-LN assisted Orka with handing over the merchandise. The gorg sat upon G-LN's head before leaping to the desk, where<ref name="Recruit" /> he<ref name="Dangerous Business">{{Resistance|Dangerous Business}}</ref> was observed by G-LN.<ref name="Recruit" />

[[File:GLNShovesXiono-TheTripleDark.png|thumb|left|250px|G-LN finishes shoving Kazuda Xiono.]]
On another [[Standard day|day]], BB-8 and Xiono fell through a chute into Acquisitions while avoiding the [[Aleena]] [[Grevel]], to whom Xiono owed credits. G-LN and his owners gazed down at Xiono as he righted himself. As Flix critiqued Xiono's decision not to use the front door, G-LN began pushing Xiono out from behind the desk. Xiono and the shopkeepers discussed the spy's need to purchase a [[ZX-19 compressor]] while G-LN finished directing him to the front of Acquisitions.<ref name="Triple">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref>

On the morning Flix, G-LN, and Orka were to visit [[Flix's mother]], the three walked through Acquisitions with Flix motioning for G-LN, carrying luggage, to follow. When Xiono arrived to watch over the store, G-LN stood nearby while Flix and Orka explained the business's motions. As the group left for the day, the pit droid beeped at Xiono until he moved and followed Flix and Orka out. Later that night, G-LN returned to Acquisitions, carry luggage again, with Flix and Orka as the partners argued about Flix's [[parent]]s. G-LN was startled upon seeing the Office destroyed, from a scuffle between BB-8 and [[thief]] [[Teroj Kee]]. The droid left rather than listen to Xiono's explanation<ref name="Dangerous Business" />

===Misadventures===
{{Quote|Poor G-LN looks bored.''"<br />"''Yeah. I got something for you, little guy. Here, have a sip of my Blurrgfire.|Flix and Orka|<ref name="G-LN" />}}
Later, G-LN was in Acquisitions carrying a box while Flix and Orka attempted to open a box they had obtained from the salvager [[Synara San]]. The shopkeepers accidentally activated the [[thermal detonator]]s inside after opening it but the devices failed to explode. the partners soon after removed the [[bomb]]s from the shop.<ref name="Treasure Chest">{{Resistance|Treasure Chest}}</ref> Another [[Galactic Standard Time|time]], Flix, G-LN, and Orka sat together at the bar in [[Aunt Z's Tavern]]. When Flix remarked that G-LN looked bored, Orka poured some of his [[Blurrgfire]] into the droid's bowl. G-LN consumed the drink while Flix and Orka conversed with [[Z'Vk'Thkrkza]], an old friend of theirs<ref name="G-LN" /> and "Aunt Z" of the [[Cantina|tavern]].<ref name="Recruit" /> The pit droid burped a few times before shrieking in excitement. While his owners conversed, the droid ran amok the cantina and knocked a tray from an [[Unidentified astromech droid|astromech droid]], kicked a tray and cup away from the [[Klatooinian]] [[Bolza Grool]], and stole a ladle from<ref name="G-LN" /> cantina's [[service droid]]<ref name="USWNE" /> [[G1-7CH]].<ref name="G-LN" />

The assaulted droids and Grool chased G-LN around the cantina before the pit droid was cornered on a table. As G-LN waved the ladle back and forth, Grool grabbed the small droid's neck and punched his head, deactivating him. As the trio left his unconcious body on the table, Flix inquired to Orka how G-LN was. Orka watched the droid's body slide off the table and joked he looked down, which Flix did not find funny.<ref name="G-LN" />

===Avoiding the First Order===
During the [[First Order]]'s [[Occupation of the Colossus|occupation]] of the ''Colossus'', G-LN hid&mdash;along with Flix, Orka, and their pet gorg Bitey&mdash;from the First Order inside a crate. The crate was scheduled to be delivered by the [[First Order delivery service]] to [[Flix's mother's home]] on [[Talivar]]. After days of hiding, Xiono discovered the group in the crate after hearing sounds from Acquisitions. As Bitey sat on his head, G-LN watched Xiono discuss with Flix and Orka his plans to fight the First Order and their plans to go to Talivar. After Xiono informed the group the [[Space station|station]] was under[[water]], Flix and Orka wished the Resistance member luck before closing the crate's lid again.<ref name="No Escape">{{Resistance|No Escape: Part 1}}</ref>

Later into 34 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="S2">{{ResistanceDate|2}}</ref> after the ''Colossus'' left Castilon and spent [[Standard month|months]] [[Hunt for the Colossus|fleeing]] from the First Order,<ref name="No Place">{{Resistance|No Place Safe}}</ref> [[Imanuel Doza]]&mdash;[[Captain]] of the ''Colossus''&mdash;settled the station on the planet [[Aeos Prime]]. As Doza announced the new home to the citizens, G-LN gathered with Flix, Orka, and many others in the [[Colossus marketplace|marketplace]] as the [[Blast door|shield doors]] revealed Aeos.<ref name="New">{{Resistance|The New World}}</ref> During the [[Battle of Barabesh|rescue]] of [[Tamara Ryvora]], G-LN took up [[Blaster pistol|arms]] to stand his ground and face the First Order's [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer]] ''[[Thunderer]]'', which had been [[Hunt for the Colossus|pursuing]] them through space.<ref name="The Escape">{{Resistance|The Escape (episode)}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
G-LN was programmed to serve his masters Flix and Orka. He spoke [[Binary]]. He had an amicable relationship with them. One one occasion, Orka rewarded him by serving him Blurrgfire, which caused him to go on a rampage and pick a fight with other patrons.<ref name="G-LN" />

==Behind the scenes==
G-LN first appeared, albeit unnamed, in part two of the two-part episode "[[The Recruit]],"<ref name="Recruit" /> the first episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', which aired on [[October 7]], [[2018]].<ref name="Disney release">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> G-LN's sounds were sourced from those created by<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|username=DavidWCollins|url=status/1622624622482194434|name=[[David W. Collins]]|date=2023-02-06|quote=These were made by Ben Burtt originally for The Phantom Menace. Pretty sure they were a combination of processed monkeys and squeak toy recordings. {{C|@DavidWCollins Do you remember how you made G-LN's squeaks and squeals? I love pit droids so much. #StarWarsResistance"}}|archiveurl=https://archive.is/cKCFE}}</ref> [[Lucasfilm]] sound designer<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> [[Ben Burtt]] for the pit droids in [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode 1 ''The Phantom Menace'']],<ref name="Twitter" /> the [[prequel trilogy]] film that released in [[1999]].<ref name="TPM" /> 

The droid was initially identified as "GL-N" in his [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry on [[StarWars.com]], which was posted online by [[October 15]], 2018.<ref name="ID">{{WookCite|url=G-LN?oldid=7933660|text=October 15, 2018 revision of the G-LN article}}</ref> However, the short "[[G-LN (episode)|G-LN]],"<ref name="G-LN" /> which released [[December 17]] of that year,<ref name="YouTube">{{DisneyYouTube|Ym78SA4gxZM|G-LN &#124; Star Wars Resistance &#124; Disney Channel|date=2018-12-17}}</ref> identified the droid as "G-LN."<ref name="G-LN" /> [[2019 Topps Star Wars Resistance|2019 Topps ''Star Wars Resistance'' Surprise Packs]]<ref name="Error">{{Topps|set=2019 Topps Star Wars Resistance|cardname=GL-N Earns his Keep|link=https://www.tcdb.com/viewcard.cfm/sid/202161/cid/12883891}}</ref>&mdash;released [[April 10]], 2019<ref name="Topps">{{WebCite|url=https://www.beckett.com/news/2019-topps-star-wars-resistance-surprise-packs|text=2019 Topps ''Star Wars Resistance'' Surprise Packs Checklist, Details, Date|work=[[Wikipedia:Beckett Media|Beckett Media]]|author=Ryan Cracknell|date=2019-04-06|oldversion=20220817140801}}</ref>&mdash;returned to "GL-N" and also misstated that G-LN worked in [[Jarek Yeager's Repair Station]] to restore the ''[[Fireball]]''.<ref name="Error" /> "[[Resistance Revisited|''Resistance'' Revisited]]," an article within [[Star Wars Insider 190|''Star Wars Insider'' 190]]<ref name="RR" /> that released on [[June 12]], 2019,<ref name="Insider 190 PREVIEWSworld">{{TitanComics|url=m/2-star-wars-insider-190|text=Star Wars Insider #190}}</ref> employed the "G-LN" spelling again.<ref name="RR" /> By [[July 18]] of that year, the Databank entry was changed to match the short.<ref name="Change">{{Databank|g-ln|G-LN}}</ref> On [[October 4]], 2019,<ref name="Penguin">{{PenguinRandomHouse|url=books/608236/ultimate-star-wars-new-edition-by-adam-bray|text=Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition}}</ref> the reference book ''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]'' returned "GL-N" to use.<ref name="USWNE" /> Finally, [[De Agostini]]'s ''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia]]'' reused "G-LN" with the "[[Ace Squadron (reference book)|Ace Squadron]]" booklet,<ref name="Ace" /> which published on [[May 27]], [[2022]].<ref name="Ace Release">{{Altaya|url=livres-bd/encyclopedie-star-wars|text=Encyclopédie Star Wars - Livres}}</ref>

